# Everything the aihub-onnx-models-runner base image installs on top of the aihub
# framework's requirements-base.txt, listed explicitly: requirements.txt is compiled
# from this file with --no-deps and installed with `pip install --no-deps --require-hashes`,
# so only these packages, at these versions, with these hashes, end up in the image. Lock for
# the container target (linux aarch64, CPython 3.13, the python:3.13-slim base of python-slim):
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --no-deps --python-platform aarch64-manylinux_2_34 \
#       --python-version 3.13 --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
#
# Transitive dependencies deliberately left out: sympy + mpmath (~80 MB, only used by
# onnxruntime's offline tooling) and coloredlogs + humanfriendly (declared by the plugin
# wheel, never imported at runtime).
#
# opencv-python-headless is here rather than in a runner because the `aihub` framework
# itself needs cv2 - the websocket input decodes frames with it - so every runner on this
# base needs it too. One ~90 MB wheel in the base instead of one per runner.
#
# onnxruntime-qnn is a plugin EP compiled against one onnxruntime release and one QAIRT
# release, and it bundles that QAIRT (~190 MB of libQnnHtp*.so plus the Hexagon skels). That
# bundled QAIRT is the only one in this image - unlike qairt-common-base, python-slim ships no
# QAIRT SDK of its own - so the wheel decides the QAIRT the NPU runs, and the HTP context
# binaries a runner ships have to be compiled against it.
#
# Pairs, from the release notes (https://github.com/onnxruntime/onnxruntime-qnn/releases) and
# measured on the 21q with the EasyOCR recognizer:
#   2.5.0 -> ORT 1.29.0, QAIRT 2.49.40   correct (pinned)
#
# The line below records the QAIRT of the pinned wheel. It is read by
# tests/containers/ai/test_ocr_runner_context_binaries.py and compared with the `qnn_version`
# recorded in every runner's models/**/*.qnn_ctx.json, so bumping the wheel without
# recompiling the context binaries turns CI red.
# qairt-version: 2.49.40
numpy==2.5.3
onnxruntime==1.29.0
onnxruntime-qnn==2.5.0
flatbuffers==25.12.19
protobuf==7.36.1
packaging==26.3
opencv-python-headless==5.0.0.93
